<title>USA: Yellen-jobs data show US economy on solid footing.</title>
<headline>Yellen-jobs data show US economy on solid footing.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton's top economic adviser said Friday that new jobless data was evidence that the U.S. economy was on a &quot;solid footing&quot; for continued job creation and economic growth.</p>
<p>&quot;With a falling deficit, low and stable inflation, and lean inventories, our economy remains on solid footing for continued job creation and economic growth, with all Americans increasingly sharing in the benefits of that growth,&quot; said Janet Yellen, chair of Clinton's Council of Economic Advisers.</p>
</text>
